# =============================================================================
# SECRETS EXAMPLE (retired) - see secrets.sops.yml.example
# =============================================================================
# The Ansible Vault is retired (decouple-manager-sops 2.11): secrets now live
# in inventory/group_vars/all/secrets.sops.yml (SOPS + age). This file was the
# old vault template and is kept only as a pointer.
#
# The full secrets template with every live key and placeholder values is:
#   inventory/group_vars/all/secrets.sops.yml.example
# (copy it to secrets.sops.yml, fill the placeholders, `make sops-encrypt`;
#  `make sops-init` copies the same template).
#
# The vault file inventory/group_vars/all/secrets.yml still exists ONLY for
# the tailscale trio until key expiry (OPERATIONS_RUNBOOK §7.4):
#
#   # tailscale_auth_key: "tskey-auth-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX"     (node join)
#   # tailscale_acl_key: "tskey-client-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX"    (ACL automation)
#   # tailscale_acl_client_id: "your-oauth-client-id"       (paired with above)
#
# Do NOT create a new vault file; use the SOPS workflow above.
# =============================================================================
